# Morass Roleplay — development rules

Full context: `docs/AI_DEVELOPER_CONTEXT.md`

## Non-negotiables

- **Performance first** — large player counts. No per-frame hooks, net spam, or `player.GetAll()` in hot paths without strong reason.
- **Reuse Helix** — factions, classes, items, attributes, meta, hooks, libs, plugins. Never duplicate inventory, money, chat, or persistence.
- **Schema only** — gameplay code in `gamemodes/morass/schema/`. Do not edit `gamemodes/helix/` for schema behaviour; override via hooks/meta.
- **Human code** — match existing file conventions. No tutorial comments, section banners, or over-engineered validation on framework objects.
- **Addons** — convert to Helix patterns; strip lag (scoped effects, timer-based logic, remove junk HUDs/autorun). No raw Workshop drops.

## Code placement

| Feature | Location |
|---------|----------|
| Jobs | `schema/factions/`, `schema/classes/` |
| Items | `schema/items/` |
| Hooks | `cl_hooks.lua`, `sh_hooks.lua`, `sv_hooks.lua` |
| Shared logic | `schema/libs/` |
| Char/player API | `schema/meta/` |

